# WHYspace Program Model

## What is a Program?

A **program** in WHYspace is a self-contained AI-native application that runs within the spatial desktop environment. Each program has its own UI, its own system prompt context, and communicates through system calls.

Programs are the **killer feature** — they transform WHYspace from a chatbot into an operating system.

---

## Program Interface

```typescript
interface ProgramManifest {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  version: string;
  description: string;
  author?: string;
  icon: string;           // icon name or URL
  category: ProgramCategory;

  // Window defaults
  defaultWindow: {
    width: number;
    height: number;
    minWidth?: number;
    minHeight?: number;
    resizable?: boolean;
  };

  // System prompt fragment injected into kernel
  systemPrompt?: string;

  // Capabilities this program needs
  permissions: Permission[];

  // Commands exposed to palette
  commands: CommandDef[];

  // Icon component path
  componentPath: string;
}

type ProgramCategory =
  | 'communication'
  | 'development'
  | 'knowledge'
  | 'creative'
  | 'automation'
  | 'system';

type Permission =
  | 'ai:chat'
  | 'ai:vision'
  | 'ai:audio'
  | 'memory:read'
  | 'memory:write'
  | 'fs:read'
  | 'fs:write'
  | 'program:launch'
  | 'workflow:execute'
  | 'network';
```

---

## Built-in Programs

### 1. Core Chat

```
ID: core-chat
Category: communication
System Prompt: General-purpose conversational AI assistant
Capabilities: ai:chat, memory:read, memory:write
```

The flagship conversational interface. Supports:
- Multi-turn conversations with full context
- Markdown rendering with code highlighting
- File/image upload with automatic analysis
- Conversation branching
- Context-aware follow-ups

### 2. Code Studio

```
ID: code-studio
Category: development
System Prompt: Expert programming AI with full-stack knowledge
Capabilities: ai:chat, ai:vision, memory:read, memory:write, fs:read, fs:write
```

AI pair programmer with integrated code editor:
- Monaco Editor with syntax highlighting
- Multi-language support (Python, JS, TS, Java, C++, Go, Rust, SQL)
- AI code generation, review, and refactoring
- Execute code in sandboxed environment
- Git integration
- File tree browser

### 3. Research Agent

```
ID: research-agent
Category: knowledge
System Prompt: Deep research AI with analytical reasoning
Capabilities: ai:chat, memory:read, memory:write, fs:read
```

Deep research and analysis tool:
- Multi-source research synthesis
- Structured report generation
- Source comparison and bias detection
- Citation management
- Export to PDF/Markdown
- Follow-up question generation

### 4. Memory Vault

```
ID: memory-vault
Category: knowledge
System Prompt: Knowledge management and retrieval AI
Capabilities: memory:read, memory:write, ai:chat
```

Visual knowledge management:
- Knowledge graph visualization
- Semantic search interface
- Memory browser with filters
- Tag and category management
- Import/export memories
- Timeline view

### 5. Image Forge

```
ID: image-forge
Category: creative
System Prompt: Creative AI artist and image editor
Capabilities: ai:vision, ai:chat, fs:read, fs:write
```

AI image generation and editing:
- Text-to-image generation (DALL-E, Gemini)
- Image editing and inpainting
- Style transfer
- Batch generation
- Gallery view
- Prompt history and refinement

### 6. Voice Nexus

```
ID: voice-nexus
Category: communication
System Prompt: Voice interaction AI assistant
Capabilities: ai:audio, ai:chat
```

Voice interaction hub:
- Speech-to-text with live transcription
- Text-to-speech with multiple voices
- Voice activity detection
- Audio file transcription
- Multi-language support
- Voice commands

### 7. Workflow Automator

```
ID: workflow-automator
Category: automation
System Prompt: Workflow automation and orchestration AI
Capabilities: ai:chat, memory:read, memory:write, workflow:execute, program:launch
```

Visual workflow builder:
- Drag-and-drop workflow editor
- Pre-built template library
- Trigger system (time, event, manual)
- Step chaining with data transformation
- Error handling and retry logic
- Execution logs and monitoring

### 8. AI Terminal

```
ID: ai-terminal
Category: development
System Prompt: Technical AI with shell and system expertise
Capabilities: ai:chat, fs:read, fs:write, program:launch
```

Natural language command line:
- Shell-like interface
- Natural language to command translation
- System call direct access
- Script execution
- Command history
- Output streaming

---

## Program Lifecycle

```
INSTALLED → LAUNCHED → ACTIVE → BACKGROUND → TERMINATED
                ↓                           ↑
            HIBERNATED ──────────────────────┘
```

| State | Description |
|---|---|
| `INSTALLED` | Program registered but not running |
| `LAUNCHING` | Initializing, loading resources |
| `ACTIVE` | Has window focus, receiving input |
| `BACKGROUND` | Running but no focus |
| `HIBERNATED` | State saved, minimal resources |
| `TERMINATED` | Stopped, resources freed |

---

## Building Custom Programs

Third-party programs follow the same interface. A program is just a directory with a `manifest.json` and a React component:

```
my-program/
├── manifest.json     # ProgramManifest
├── icon.svg          # Program icon
├── index.tsx         # Main component
└── styles.css        # Optional styles
```

### manifest.json

```json
{
  "id": "my-custom-tutor",
  "name": "AI Tutor Pro",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Personalized tutoring across all subjects",
  "author": "Community",
  "icon": "graduation-cap",
  "category": "knowledge",
  "defaultWindow": { "width": 700, "height": 500 },
  "systemPrompt": "You are an expert tutor...",
  "permissions": ["ai:chat", "memory:read", "memory:write"],
  "commands": [
    { "id": "tutor.quiz", "label": "Generate Quiz", "params": {} }
  ]
}
```

### Component Template

```tsx
import { useProgram, useSyscall } from '@whyspace/kernel';

export default function AITutorPro() {
  const { pid, window } = useProgram();
  const syscall = useSyscall();

  const handleAsk = async (question: string) => {
    const stream = syscall('ai.stream', {
      messages: [{ role: 'user', content: question }],
      system: 'You are an expert tutor...'
    });

    for await (const chunk of stream) {
      // render chunk.data
    }
  };

  return (
    <div className="p-4">
      <h1>AI Tutor Pro</h1>
      {/* your UI */}
    </div>
  );
}
```
